    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get both sides, but look at the data from some of the European countries that tried it. It seems like the capital flight and the lack of investment part actually happens more often than the inequality part gets fixed. Wouldn't you say that from an economic standpoint, the risk of stifling growth is a more proven outcome than the benefit of redistribution?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
